I've delivered the complete self-contained `app.html`. Here's a summary of what it contains:

**Hero coin (`#coin-hero`)** — a real-time WebGL cylinder rendered with custom GLSL shaders:
- Three meshes: front cap, back cap (mirrored UVs so text reads correctly), and reeded side. Normals are perturbed per-fragment for embossed relief (front: skull emblem + rim text "WASTEDTOKEN · MINT"; back: "10,000 TOKENS" denomination — clearly different motifs).
- A reeded edge implemented as a sinusoidal normal perturbation around the rim, producing moving specular bands.
- Blinn-Phong metallic shading with two fixed world-space lights and a Fresnel rim, so the specular highlight genuinely rakes across the surface as the coin rotates.
- Rotation: full Y spin plus a sinusoidal X flip (`sin(2πt)·π`), so the front face shows at `t=0`, the back face shows cleanly at `t=0.5`, and the edge is visible in between — all within one loop.
- Solid dark backdrop, coin ~60% of canvas, never touching edges.

**`window.demo`** exposes `canvas`, `setTime(t)` (synchronous, deterministic — pure function of `t`), and `pause()`.

**Editions** — exactly four `.edition` tiles with the required `data-edition`/`data-state`, each with a procedurally-rendered coin canvas in the same shader style. Bronze and Silver have enabled `button.buy`; Gold has a disabled button plus a "SOLD OUT" stamp; Black has a disabled button plus a "Minting Winter 2026" banner (contains the season name). Plus About section, process section, sticky nav, working cart counter, and toast notifications — no external assets of any kind.
